IOF ATTRIBUTION LICENSE
Version 1.0

1. OVERVIEW AND INTENT
The Infinite Optical Fabric (IOF) Attribution License is a permissive instrument designed to
encourage the open development, simulation, and hardware implementation of resonance-
based optical systems. This license ensures that while the Work is free to evolve across all
sectors—including private, commercial, governmental, and defense—the foundational
intellectual contribution remains recognized.

2. PERMITTED ACTIONS
Subject to the condition in Section 3, any individual, organization, or automated system is
granted a perpetual, worldwide, royalty-free right to:

• Reproduce, modify, and create derivative works of the IOF concepts, simulations,
  and code.
• Incorporate the Work into physical hardware, defense systems, or shielding
  technologies.
• Utilize the Work for the training, fine-tuning, and prompt-engineering of Artificial
  Intelligence (AI) and Machine Learning (ML) models.

3. THE ATTRIBUTION REQUIREMENT
Any public distribution, derivative work, or implementation must include the following
attribution string in a clear and conspicuous manner (e.g., in source code headers,
documentation, "About" screens, or AI metadata tags):

"Infinite Optical Fabric by Gregory Scott Davis, Princeton, NC."

4. LIMITATION OF LIABILITY
THE WORK IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR
IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY OR
FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE AUTHOR BE LIABLE
FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES, OR OTHER LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF
CONTRACT, TORT, OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM, OUT OF, OR IN CONNECTION WITH
THE WORK OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE WORK.

